// Core AI ComputeStream test (16 Nov 2026): the split decode verify with the ANE calls ENCODED onto a ComputeStream that
// wraps the GPU engine's own Metal queue (dec_gpu.swift's `queue`), the GPU attention command buffers committed on that
// queue between them, and ONE wait per step (no CPU round trip per handoff). Probe 2's entries (dva0, dvba, dvb1,
// v8_16k..96k); the GPU reads a synthetic INT8 KV cache in the 96K ladder. Generated by gen.py (main.tmpl.swift).
// Per N keys: a 16-chunk step as  ref (16 x v8_<entry>, stream)  |  fused stream (dva0, 15 x (GPU, dvba), GPU, dvb1; one
// wait)  |  fused sync (the same with a CPU wait after every call)  |  ANE parts only (stream)  |  GPU parts only.
// Correctness: the fused stream's y must equal the fused sync's y bit for bit (every chain buffer zeroed before each run).
//   python3 gen.py PROBE2 > main.swift && swiftc -O -swift-version 5 -o dec_stream main.swift ../../engine/dec_gpu.swift \
//     -framework Metal -framework QuartzCore && ./dec_stream PROBE2/chunks_L00-07.aimodel ../../engine/dec_kernels.metal
import CoreAI
import Foundation
